> float c;
> 
> float divide ( int x, int y)
> {
>         c = (float) (x/y);
>         return c;
> }

	Hmm, I think you want

	c = ((float)(x))/((float)(y));

Otherwise, the division will be done first as integers, giving an integer
quotient, which you're then turning into a float.

